    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_5_1"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "4.5.1" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Cost-effectiveness results should reflect the present value of the stream of costs and benefits accruing over the time horizon of the analysis. For the reference case, costs and health effects should be discounted at the same rate of 3.5% per year." .

heiro:5000177 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 4.5.2, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_5_2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "4.5.2" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Alternative analyses using rates of 1.5% for both costs and health effects may be presented alongside the reference-case analysis, in specific circumstances." .

heiro:5000178 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 4.5.3, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_5_3"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "4.5.3" ;
    heiro:2000007 "The committee may consider analyses using a non-reference-case discount rate of 1.5% per year for both costs and health effects, if, in the committee's considerations, all of the following criteria are met: The technology is for people who would otherwise die or have a very severely impaired life. It is likely to restore them to full or near-full health. The benefits are likely to be sustained over a very long period." .

heiro:5000180 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 4.2.7, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_2_7"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "4.2.7" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For the reference case, the perspective on outcomes should be all relevant health effects, whether for patients or, when relevant, other people (mainly carers). The perspective adopted on costs should be that of the NHS and PSS." .

heiro:5000182 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 4.2.14, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/economic-evaluation-2#pmg36-4_2_14"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "4.2.14" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Cost-effectiveness (specifically cost-utility) analysis is used to determine if differences in expected costs between technologies can be justified in terms of changes in expected health effects. Health effects should be expressed in terms of quality-adjusted life years (QALYs) ." .

heiro:5000184 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 2.2.12, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/the-scope-2#pmg36-2_2_12"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "2.2.12" ;
    heiro:2000007 "The scope identifies all potentially relevant comparators that are established practice in the NHS. It considers issues likely to be discussed by the committee when selecting the most appropriate comparator. At this stage of the evaluation, identifying comparators should be inclusive." .

heiro:5000185 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 2.2.15, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/the-scope-2#pmg36-2_2_15"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "2.2.15" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Technologies that NICE has recommended with managed access are not considered established practice in the NHS and are not considered suitable comparators." .

heiro:5000189 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.7, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_3_7"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.7" ;
    heiro:2000007 "As the ICER for a technology increases in the range of £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY gained, the committee's decisions about the acceptability of the technology as an effective use of NHS resources will make explicit reference to the relevant factors listed in section 6.3.5." .

heiro:5000190 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.8, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_3_8"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.8" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Above a most plausible ICER of £35,000 per QALY gained or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, the committee will need to identify an increasingly stronger case for supporting the technology as an effective use of NHS resources, considering the factors listed in sections 6.3.5 and 6.3.6." .

heiro:5000193 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.2, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_3_2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.2" ;
    heiro:2000007 "To be transparent in decision making, when applying decision-making modifiers, net health benefits should be routinely presented to show the effect on opportunity costs of recommending a technology that meets specific decision-making modifiers. Net health benefits should be presented using values placed on a QALY gain of £25,000 and £35,000, both with and without the QALY weighting applied. Positive net health benefits mean that overall population health is increased because of the new technology. Negative net health benefits mean that the health benefits associated with the new technology are not large enough to prevent overall health loss because of healthcare not being funded elsewhere in the system. Technologies associated with negative unweighted net health benefits may still be recommended when decision-making modifiers have been applied. This is because there is an ethical and moral rationale to value the health benefits gained with these technologies more than those gained by technologies not meeting decision-making modifiers." .

heiro:5000195 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.2.18, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_2_18"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.2.18" ;
    heiro:2000007 "The QALY weightings for severity are applied based on absolute and proportional shortfall, whichever implies the greater severity level. If either the proportional or absolute QALY shortfall calculated falls on the cut-off between severity levels, the higher severity level will apply." .

heiro:5000196 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 table 6.1, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "table 6.1" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Table 6.1 QALY weightings for severity QALY weight Proportional QALY shortfall Absolute QALY shortfall 1 Less than 0.85 Less than 12 x1.2 0.85 to 0.95 12 to 18 x1.7 At least 0.95 At least 18" .

heiro:5000198 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.2.20, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_2_20"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.2.20" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For highly specialised technologies, the severity of the condition is already implicitly captured in the selection of technologies for evaluations. No additional QALY weighting for the severity of disease is applied." .

heiro:5000200 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.2.22, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_2_22"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.2.22" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For highly specialised technologies, the committee will consider the size of the incremental QALY gain in relation to the additional weight that would need to be assigned to the QALY benefits for the cost effectiveness of the technology to fall within the highly specialised technologies £100,000 cost per QALY level." .

heiro:5000201 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.2.23, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_2_23"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.2.23" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For this weight to be applied, there will need to be compelling evidence that the treatment offers significant QALY gains. Depending on the number of QALYs gained over the lifetime of patients, when comparing the new technology with its relevant comparator(s), the committee will apply a weight between 1 and 3, using equal increments, for a range between 10 and 30 QALYs gained." .

heiro:5000205 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.7, version of 17 December 2025"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000142 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.7" ;
    heiro:2000007 "As the ICER for a technology increases in the range of £20,000 to £30,000 per QALY gained, the committee's decisions about the acceptability of the technology as an effective use of NHS resources will make explicit reference to the relevant factors listed in section 6.3.5." .

heiro:5000206 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.8, version of 17 December 2025"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000142 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.8" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Above a most plausible ICER of £30,000 per QALY gained or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, the committee will need to identify an increasingly stronger case for supporting the technology as an effective use of NHS resources, considering the factors listed in sections 6.3.5 and 6.3.6." .

heiro:5000208 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG51 section 1.7, version of 27 August 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000151 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg51/chapter/statement-on-using-the-eq-5d-5l-value-set"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "1.7" ;
    heiro:2000007 "After this interim methods statement is published, the EQ-5D-5L descriptive system and the new UK value set will be NICE's preferred approaches to measure and value health-related quality of life in adults." .

heiro:5000212 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "Value Assessment Framework section 3.6, version of 25 September 2023"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000162 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://icer.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/ICER_2023_2026_VAF_070126.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "3.6" ;
    heiro:2000007 "discounting of both costs and outcomes, at the rate of 3% per year." .

heiro:5000214 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "Value Assessment Framework section 3.9, version of 25 September 2023"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000162 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://icer.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/ICER_2023_2026_VAF_070126.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "3.9" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Price Benchmarks remains $100,000-$150,000 per evLY and per QALY" .

heiro:5000216 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "Choices in methods for economic evaluation Guideline 7, version of 29 July 2020"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000167 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.has-sante.fr/upload/docs/application/pdf/2020-11/methodological_guidance_2020_-choices_in_methods_for_economic_evaluation.pdf"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "Guideline 7" ;
    heiro:2000007 "the public discount rate applicable at the time of the evaluation (set at 2.5% at the time of publication of this guidance)" .

heiro:5000218 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PBAC Guidelines section 3A.1.5, version of September 2016"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000172 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://pbac.pbs.gov.au/section-3a/3a-1-overview-and-rationale-of-economic-evaluation.html"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "3A.1.5" ;
    heiro:2000007 "annual (compounding) rate of 5% per year for all costs and health outcomes that occur" .

heiro:5000221 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.7, version of 31 March 2026"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000145 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.7" ;
    heiro:2000007 "As the ICER for a technology increases in the range of £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY gained, the committee's decisions about the acceptability of the technology as an effective use of NHS resources will make explicit reference to the relevant factors listed in section 6.3.5." .

heiro:5000222 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.8, version of 31 March 2026"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000145 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.8" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Above a most plausible ICER of £35,000 per QALY gained or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, the committee will need to identify an increasingly stronger case for supporting the technology as an effective use of NHS resources, considering the factors listed in sections 6.3.5 and 6.3.6." .

heiro:5000253 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 2.2.13, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/the-scope-2#pmg36-2_2_13"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "2.2.13" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Comparator technologies may include branded and non-proprietary (generic) medicines and biosimilars. They may also include technologies that do not have regulatory approval for the population defined in the scope if they are considered to be established clinical practice for the population in the NHS." .

heiro:5000254 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.2.21, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_2_21"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.2.21" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Technologies recommended after applying the severity modifier will be considered as relevant comparators for future evaluations of new technologies introduced for the same condition. They must have been recommended for routine use and represent established practice in the NHS at the time of evaluating the new technology. Second and subsequent extensions to the regulatory approval for the same technology will be considered on their individual merits." .

heiro:5000257 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.2, version of 31 March 2026"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000145 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.2" ;
    heiro:2000007 "To be transparent in decision making, when applying decision-making modifiers, net health benefits should be routinely presented to show the effect on opportunity costs of recommending a technology that meets specific decision-making modifiers. Net health benefits should be presented using values placed on a QALY gain of £25,000 and £35,000, both with and without the QALY weighting applied. Positive net health benefits mean that overall population health is increased because of the new technology. Negative net health benefits mean that the health benefits associated with the new technology are not large enough to prevent overall health loss because of healthcare not being funded elsewhere in the system. Technologies associated with negative unweighted net health benefits may still be recommended when decision-making modifiers have been applied. This is because there is an ethical and moral rationale to value the health benefits gained with these technologies more than those gained by technologies not meeting decision-making modifiers." .

heiro:5000259 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.9, version of 31 March 2026"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000145 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260618195253id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.9" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For technologies that provide less health benefit at a lower cost compared with the relevant comparator(s) (that is, that fall in the south-west quadrant of a cost-effectiveness plane), cost-effectiveness considerations should consider the usual cost-effectiveness levels of £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY. Any relevant additional factors and modifiers should also be taken into account." .

heiro:5000260 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.9, version of 13 October 2026"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000148 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2#pmg36-6_3_9"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.9" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For technologies that provide less health benefit at a lower cost compared with the relevant comparator(s) (that is, that fall in the south-west quadrant of a cost-effectiveness plane), cost-effectiveness considerations should consider the usual cost-effectiveness levels of £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY. Any relevant additional factors and modifiers should also be taken into account." .

heiro:5000263 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.7, version of 31 January 2022"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000127 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.7" ;
    heiro:2000007 "As the ICER for a technology increases in the range of £20,000 to £30,000 per QALY gained, the committee's decisions about the acceptability of the technology as an effective use of NHS resources will make explicit reference to the relevant factors listed in section 6.3.5." .

heiro:5000264 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.8, version of 31 January 2022"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000127 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.8" ;
    heiro:2000007 "Above a most plausible ICER of £30,000 per QALY gained or £100,000 per QALY gained for highly specialised technologies, the committee will need to identify an increasingly stronger case for supporting the technology as an effective use of NHS resources, considering the factors listed in sections 6.3.5 and 6.3.6." .

heiro:5000266 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.2, version of 31 January 2022"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000127 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.2" ;
    heiro:2000007 "To be transparent in decision making, when applying decision-making modifiers, net health benefits should be routinely presented to show the effect on opportunity costs of recommending a technology that meets specific decision-making modifiers. Net health benefits should be presented using values placed on a QALY gain of £20,000 and £30,000, both with and without the QALY weighting applied. Positive net health benefits mean that overall population health is increased because of the new technology. Negative net health benefits mean that the health benefits associated with the new technology are not large enough to prevent overall health loss because of healthcare not being funded elsewhere in the system. Technologies associated with negative unweighted net health benefits may still be recommended when decision-making modifiers have been applied. This is because there is an ethical and moral rationale to value the health benefits gained with these technologies more than those gained by technologies not meeting decision-making modifiers." .

heiro:5000267 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.2, version of 17 December 2025"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000142 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.2" ;
    heiro:2000007 "To be transparent in decision making, when applying decision-making modifiers, net health benefits should be routinely presented to show the effect on opportunity costs of recommending a technology that meets specific decision-making modifiers. Net health benefits should be presented using values placed on a QALY gain of £20,000 and £30,000, both with and without the QALY weighting applied. Positive net health benefits mean that overall population health is increased because of the new technology. Negative net health benefits mean that the health benefits associated with the new technology are not large enough to prevent overall health loss because of healthcare not being funded elsewhere in the system. Technologies associated with negative unweighted net health benefits may still be recommended when decision-making modifiers have been applied. This is because there is an ethical and moral rationale to value the health benefits gained with these technologies more than those gained by technologies not meeting decision-making modifiers." .

heiro:5000269 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.9, version of 31 January 2022"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000127 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20220809045402id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.9" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For technologies that provide less health benefit at a lower cost compared with the relevant comparator(s) (that is, that fall in the south-west quadrant of a cost-effectiveness plane), cost-effectiveness considerations should consider the usual cost-effectiveness levels of £20,000 to £30,000 per QALY. Any relevant additional factors and modifiers should also be taken into account." .

heiro:5000270 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 6.3.9, version of 17 December 2025"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000142 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20260222032810id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/committee-recommendations-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "6.3.9" ;
    heiro:2000007 "For technologies that provide less health benefit at a lower cost compared with the relevant comparator(s) (that is, that fall in the south-west quadrant of a cost-effectiveness plane), cost-effectiveness considerations should consider the usual cost-effectiveness levels of £20,000 to £30,000 per QALY. Any relevant additional factors and modifiers should also be taken into account." .

heiro:5000272 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "PMG36 section 5.10.4, version of 31 October 2023"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Read in an archived copy of the page, https://web.archive.org/web/20250311184341id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/developing-the-guidance-2"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-register.owl> ;
    heiro:1000004 heiro:5000130 ;
    heiro:2000005 "https://web.archive.org/web/20250311184341id_/https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36/chapter/developing-the-guidance-2"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    heiro:2000006 "5.10.4" ;
    heiro:2000007 "NHS England and NHS Improvement may request a longer time to implement the statutory funding requirements for technologies funded through its specialised commissioning budgets. This may happen when the potential net budget impact is expected to exceed £20 million per year in any of the first 3 financial years of its use in the NHS. NHS England and NHS Improvement will also do this on behalf of clinical commissioning groups, for locally commissioned technologies that NICE has evaluated." .

